# The app document must not be framed (bead qrcode-22b): frame-ancestors is header-only, so a
# <meta> CSP cannot carry it, and the result panel's "Return" (x-callback) and "Open" buttons are
# clickjackable once the document can be framed. Referrer-Policy (bead qrcode-igx) keeps the app
# URL - which can carry an x-callback-url destination or a kill-switch consent token - away from
# cross-origin receivers entirely; the document also pins it in a <meta> tag for hosts that do
# not read this file.
#
# The worker responses get their own CSP (bead qrcode-7du): a <meta> CSP applies to the document
# only, so /sw.js and the decoder worker would otherwise run with no policy at all. The policies
# are scoped to the worker paths, NOT to /* on purpose: a document response CSP would COMBINE
# with the meta policy and silently kill scanning (bead qrcode-2pt). /scripts/* covers the
# worker bundle; worker dynamic-import chunks are pinned to the same tree by vite.config.js
# (worker.rollupOptions.output.chunkFileNames, guarded by test/unit/worker-csp.test.mjs -
# bead qrcode-aa0); classic scripts served from /scripts/ (main.js,
# sw-register.js) ignore their own response CSP, so the scope is inert for the document.
#
#   - /sw.js: install fetches only same-origin assets (manifest + precache), so
#     connect-src 'self' covers it; no WASM compiles in the worker global scope.
#   - /scripts/*: the decoder worker fetches scripts/zbar.wasm and compiles it, so its policy
#     MUST keep 'wasm-unsafe-eval' (its removal fails every scan with CompileError, the exact
#     regression class qrcode-2pt recorded) and connect-src 'self' for the wasm fetch.
#
# Dev/preview (vite server.headers) cannot path-scope headers, so workers stay unpoliced there;
# that residual is recorded in the stored threat model. This file is the static-host form of the
# policy (Netlify / Cloudflare Pages read `_headers`); any other host must send these headers
# itself - see the "Framing", "Referrer-Policy" and "Worker CSP" sections in README.md, the last
# of which carries the two path-scoped worker CSP values to copy.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin
/sw.js
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'
/scripts/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; connect-src 'self'
